Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Replaces the minimal MVP dialog (etName/etEmail/etUser/tilPassword/etHost/etPort/
rgEncryption/btnSave) with a full-screen editor that EXACTLY mirrors the IMAP/SMTP
FragmentAccount.java + fragment_account.xml structure:

Layout (fragment_jmap_account.xml):
- ConstraintLayout root (same as upstream, not LinearLayout)
- CardView server section: host, encryption RadioGroup (vertical SSL/STARTTLS/None),
  cbInsecure, port, user, etEmail (identity email), password with eye toggle
- name, category, color (ViewButtonColor), avatar, calendar
- btnAdvanced toggle → grpAdvanced: synchronize, ignoreSchedule, onDemand, leave link,
  primary, notify, summary, browse, autoSeen, interval, unmetered, vpnOnly
- btnCheck + pbCheck (inline JMAP connectivity test)
- grpFolders (shown after Check): spDrafts, spSent, spArchive, spTrash, spJunk,
  separator, spLeft, spRight, separator, spMove — same Barrier pattern as IMAP
- btnSave + pbSave, cbIdentity
- grpError: tvErrorTitle, tvError, btnSupport
- pbWait (initial DB load spinner)

Java (FragmentJmapAccount.java):
- ArrayAdapter<EntityFolder> adapterFolder + adapterSwipe (same as FragmentAccount)
- onActivityCreated: loads existing account+folders+identity in edit mode
- onCheck(): SimpleTask → HTTP GET /.well-known/jmap with Basic auth; on success
  calls setFolders(buildStandardFolders()) with Inbox/Drafts/Sent/Archive/Trash/Junk
- setFolders(): populates all 8 spinners, auto-selects by type, shows grpFolders+btnSave
- onSave(): full DB write — account fields + identity update + applyFolderSelections()
  to set folder types from spinners; cbIdentity navigates to FragmentIdentity on finish
- onCreateOptionsMenu/onPrepareOptionsMenu/onOptionsItemSelected: Delete (edit mode only)
- onActivityResult: color/avatar/calendar/delete (REQUEST_DELETE → SimpleTask db.deleteAccount)
